{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent","id":985145,"title":"Protection of the Innocent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T17:24:14-07:00","id":985145,"title":"Protection of the Innocent","content":"Within my games, younger children are protected from supernatural creatures because of the strength of their innocence, which I represent through using the mechanic of True Faith. Children are born with True Faith 5 but, with every year that passes, the vast majority naturally lose one level of True Faith (0-1; True Faith 5; 1-2: True Faith 4; 2-3: True Faith 3; 3-4: True Faith 2; 4-5: True Faith 1; 5+: True Faith 0). Older characters with True Faith have either retained the innocence of their youth or have acquired a new form of innocence from their faith in a religion or philosophy. I was wondering if anyone else protected younger children in a similar way in their games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:41:55-07:00","id":985156,"title":"","content":"You think that toddlers are innocent? I take it that you don't have any children.<br /> <br /> I don't do this because I feel like giving children this kind of resistance undermines the horror aspects of when supernatural evil creatures prey on children. I often do, however, allow children to sense something wrong about supernatural creatures or sometimes even see through their illusionary powers. Not as potent as True Faith, but enough of something to add an interesting twist when the Nosferatu disguising itself in front of all of the adults but the young child sees through the facade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:37:48-07:00","id":985191,"title":"","content":"I have taken care of plenty of young children throughout the years, and I have never seen evidence of evil in the hearts of young children (confusion and pain that manifested in misbehavior, but nothing that resembled evil). Older children, adolescents, and adults have evil in their heart, I have seen plenty of evidence of that, but I have never seen evidence of evil in young children. It takes time for corruption or suffering to turn people to evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:54:31-07:00","id":985199,"title":"","content":"You think that True Faith Makes someone innocent?<br /> <br /> A wicked person can become Righteous, but never innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:55:34-07:00","id":985200,"title":"","content":"That is because little kids have a power that is kind of like Presence, where they can charm you and make you think that they aren't evil. They probably used it on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:38:10-07:00","id":985219,"title":"","content":"If anything I'd say giving all children True Faith makes them <i>more</i> likely to come to supernatural harm, as any moderately intelligent and unscrupulous supernatural will quickly figure out a way to exploit such a plentiful potential asset. <br /> <br /> Insignificance is your friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:50:24-07:00","id":985224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985219#post985219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything I'd say giving all children True Faith makes them <i>more</i> likely to come to supernatural harm, as any moderately intelligent and unscrupulous supernatural will quickly figure out a way to exploit such a plentiful potential asset.<br /> <br /> Insignificance is your friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a baby with a TF of 5 is extremely dangerous. A normal baby is probably not even worth the the blood in their systems, they aren't even Masquerade witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:07:32-07:00","id":985232,"title":"","content":"Unless their opponents start throwing babies at Kindred, I do not think that a baby with True Faith 5 is particularly dangerous to most Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:20:29-07:00","id":985242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985232#post985232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless their opponents start throwing babies at Kindred, I do not think that a baby with True Faith 5 is particularly dangerous to most Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be ridiculous. You devise a high-velocity fully automatic baby launcher. <br /> <br /> Seriously, it <i>starts</i> there and only goes down hill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:24:28-07:00","id":985244,"title":"","content":"I don't give them any kind of protection, but it's been established in a lot of games that children who are still innocent can see/interact with Wraiths and many kinds of fae. They are also more attuned to the presence of supernatural evil, and thus can make an effort to avoid/hide from it.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd have powers protecting babies and such from foes in the physical plane, but I can see an argument for protection against purely spiritual forces (like Spectres and Banes).<br /> <br /> I think it is possible for older children who have retained their innocence to develop some levels of True Faith due to their unquestioning acceptance of whatever dogma they are taught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:24:33-07:00","id":985245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985242#post985242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be ridiculous. You devise a high-velocity fully automatic baby launcher.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it <i>starts</i> there and only goes down hill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what ever you do, don't introduce this idea in a hunter campaign unless you want to see babies weaponized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T23:12:11-07:00","id":985287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985245#post985245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">babies weaponized.</div> </div> </div> </div>These two words perfectly summarized my initial thoughts when I read the OP. I started picturing babies being held as shields by more twisted fanatic hunters, those same hunters raiding maturity wards for &quot;supplies in the war against EVIL&quot;, and inevitably leading to a group of kindred who start killing all pregnant women in the city as a way to &quot;disarm&quot; the hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:01:35-07:00","id":985299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985200#post985200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is because little kids have a power that is kind of like Presence, where they can charm you and make you think that they aren't evil. They probably used it on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I have known plenty of families when i was active duty who's kids (2-5) were terraways..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T03:08:34-07:00","id":985337,"title":"","content":"In mage some childs are awakened, in the sense that they are not yet asleep. They get dulled and lulled eventually and fall asleep.<br /> <br /> Have you ever wondered what stories children tell? Monsters under the bed, little rituals, etc. And they can make a gun out of a stick.<br /> <br /> Molesting random childs can get nasty real quick for your average vampire/wraith/monsterthingy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:48:31-07:00","id":985366,"title":"","content":"Hm, how would a baby make an effective shield? It is not like they could say prayers or use religious symbols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T07:29:45-07:00","id":985406,"title":"","content":"Or maybe wraith ancestors protect innocent descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T07:51:16-07:00","id":985417,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FRMiRRzJtCM\" target=\"_blank\">NAZI VAMPIRES EATING BABIES!</a><br /> <br /> (warning: exactly what it says on the tin, and also quick blinking lights.)<br /> <br /> Which is to say, where's the feeling of vulnerability if you don't have to worry about your kids? Aside from the other very valid concerns of others about hunters using babies offensively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-11-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:14:59-07:00","id":985421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985406#post985406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe wraith ancestors protect innocent descendants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be something interesting, though I think that you would have to redesign Wraith to create that effect (or you could say that the protectors are Transcended Wraiths, as their capabilities have never been specified).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:41:54-07:00","id":985443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985366#post985366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, how would a baby make an effective shield? It is not like they could say prayers or use religious symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if they can't <i>use</i> the True Faith then why even say that they have it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:38:32-07:00","id":985473,"title":"","content":"I tweak the rules a bit from chronicle to chronicle to suit the themes and mood I'm going for, and in some of them I will use something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't give them any kind of protection, but it's been established in a lot of games that children who are still innocent can see/interact with Wraiths and many kinds of fae. They are also more attuned to the presence of supernatural evil, and thus can make an effort to avoid/hide from it. </div> </div> </div>including things like resistance (but not immunity) to Obfuscate, Presence and blood bonds.<br /> <br /> But in most cases, the kids have no such luck - in fact, low-Humanity Camarilla vampires often have their tendrils deep in child trafficking, orphanages and the CPS for the precise reason that children make for convenient, defenseless Herds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:54:14-07:00","id":985511,"title":"","content":"Babies are complicated.<br /> But take a child of about 3 to 4 years. Psychology names one chapter of the childhood \u201cMagic Thinking\u201c...<br /> <br /> The stick and various \u201cb\u00e4ng\u201c \u201cka-pow\u201c noises as instrument, and the nightfolk gets fried...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:03:54-07:00","id":985580,"title":"","content":"I feel like this whole thread is predicated on our modern sensibilities where children are functionally immune to death (unless the plot specifically is about children dying). Casual child death is almost unheard of.<br /> <br /> Historically, children died <i>constantly</i>. Disease is a bitch, and often violent conflict did not spare the children either. This didn't lessen the emotional impact for the families who suffered loss, I am sure, but giving powers to kids seems absurd. Where were these magic powers prior to the 20th century?<br /> <br /> I don't have kids dying willy-nilly in my game, but it does happen. There was bitter fighting during the 1800s between the Anglos/Texians and the indigenous Comanche, Apache and others. Villages get wiped out, settlements raised, and folks die. That includes women and children too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:53:37-07:00","id":985613,"title":"","content":"That's a fair (actually, excellent) point, but I should say that I, for one, virtually exclusively run games set in modern settings (the 80s and onward) anyway. Those games get their attitudes toward children from modern stories (whether cynical or idealistic) or various gothic tropes relating to innocence and the supernatural. I agree that such treatment would be jarring in settings where the attitude toward children and childhood is very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:09:15-07:00","id":985622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985580#post985580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this whole thread is predicated on our modern sensibilities where children are functionally immune to death (unless the plot specifically is about children dying). Casual child death is almost unheard of.<br /> <br /> Historically, children died <i>constantly</i>. Disease is a bitch, and often violent conflict did not spare the children either. This didn't lessen the emotional impact for the families who suffered loss, I am sure, but giving powers to kids seems absurd. Where were these magic powers prior to the 20th century?<br /> <br /> I don't have kids dying willy-nilly in my game, but it does happen. There was bitter fighting during the 1800s between the Anglos/Texians and the indigenous Comanche, Apache and others. Villages get wiped out, settlements raised, and folks die. That includes women and children too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So pretty much this for me. I see no reason to make children specially protected.<br /> <br /> There is the point that killing/harming children generally gets more attention than killing an adult, from both law enforcement and from media. And for story purposes, if you want to make it interesting, involve the Fae. The majority of Changelings are children and so going after them has a much higher chance of the child either being a Changeling or being the friend of a Changeling. And contrary to what I've encountered as popular opinion on forums, Changelings really should not be underestimated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:53:21-07:00","id":985647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985145-protection-of-the-innocent?p=985443#post985443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if they can't <i>use</i> the True Faith then why even say that they have it?</div> </div> </div> </div>At True Faith 5, the touch of an infant would repulse Kindred. At True Faith 4, a toddler would be unable to be turned into a ghoul and would be immune to mental Disciplines. At True Faith 3, a toddler would be able to sense Kindred. At True Faith 2, a young child could spend Willpower to resist Dominate. At True Faith 1, a young child could say prayers to repel a Kindred. In addition, True Faith would add to the Willpower and Virtue rolls of the young child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:08:57-07:00","id":985663,"title":"","content":"Childrens die constantly nowadays, too.<br /> The numbers are different, and even more important the feeling and expectations are different.<br /> <br /> I know, I lost my twin daughters 4 years ago.<br /> <br /> I would not grant every child powers, not even a noteworthy percentage.<br /> But the threat of power has power itself.<br /> And even with powers (magick or otherwise) nobody is safe in the world of darkness (a child can be so scared the magick makes it worse by granting fears reality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}